WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:02.701
-Welcome back, everybody.
We're here with Bobby Flay!

00:00:02.701 --> 00:00:04.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:04.701 --> 00:00:08.367
Brasserie B opening up
in Caesars Palace in December.

00:00:08.367 --> 00:00:09.901
You're gonna make
something off that menu.

00:00:09.901 --> 00:00:11.968
This is a pork chop
you're going to teach Quest?

00:00:11.968 --> 00:00:13.300
-Yeah, so we're making --

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:15.267
So, as you know,
we like french fries.

00:00:15.267 --> 00:00:16.868
-Yeah.
-And so we're gonna make

00:00:16.868 --> 00:00:18.267
pork frite.
So we're gonna do a pork chop

00:00:18.267 --> 00:00:19.300
with french fries.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:20.701
We're gonna start
with some spice rub.

00:00:20.701 --> 00:00:22.267
You guys are gonna both do this,
okay?

00:00:22.267 --> 00:00:23.634
-Okay.
-All right. So, take the spices

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:25.100
and put them in the bowl
and mix them up.

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:26.367
-Yeah.
-So we have some --

00:00:26.367 --> 00:00:29.734
some mustard seed,
we have some some red chilies,

00:00:29.734 --> 00:00:32.100
we have coriander, paprika.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.934
Just throw it all in there,
and you're gonna season this

00:00:33.934 --> 00:00:35.400
with a little salt and pepper,
as well.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:37.634 --> 00:00:39.100
And then just season one side

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:40.801
with the -- with the --
with the spice rub.

00:00:40.801 --> 00:00:42.467
-All right. So, yeah,
just throw that on there.

00:00:42.467 --> 00:00:44.367
-Yeah. Just -- yeah.
Rub it in. Exactly.

00:00:44.367 --> 00:00:46.734
Okay. Then we're gonna take
your pork chop,

00:00:46.734 --> 00:00:48.734
and we're gonna put it
right into the -- into the pan.

00:00:48.734 --> 00:00:50.200
-Ooh. What kind of oil
you got there?

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:51.868
Grapeseed.
-This is avocado oil.

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:53.300
-Avocado, There you go.
-Good guess, though.

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:54.501
-Thank you, thank you.
Yeah, appreciate it.

00:00:54.501 --> 00:00:56.534
-Do you cook
with grapeseed oil?

00:00:56.534 --> 00:00:58.601
-No.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.601 --> 00:00:59.901
-You know what?
-No, I just drink it.

00:00:59.901 --> 00:01:01.934
-Wait a second.
You thought about lying about it

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.234
for a second.
You like grapeseed oil?

00:01:03.234 --> 00:01:05.167
"Yes, exactly.
I love that vinaigrette I make."

00:01:05.167 --> 00:01:06.868
Exactly.
-So this is avocado oil.

00:01:06.868 --> 00:01:09.367
-Yes, avocado oil.
Very nice light oil.

00:01:09.367 --> 00:01:11.267
I kind of went away from
the canola oil a little bit.

00:01:11.267 --> 00:01:12.934
I just -- you know,
they say it's better for you.

00:01:12.934 --> 00:01:13.934
I don't know.
-Oh, is that right?

00:01:13.934 --> 00:01:15.934
-Yeah. Okay.
I didn't finish

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:17.100
my book, "Fit," by Bobby Flay.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.734
-Exactly, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.501
-No spoilers.
-Exactly.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.534
-So you only put on one side.
Why not the other side?

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:23.701
-Well, only --
only on one side

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.801
'cause I still want
to taste the pork and --

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:28.434
but I do want the spices
to enhance the pork itself.

00:01:28.434 --> 00:01:29.534
Give it a little flavor.

00:01:29.534 --> 00:01:31.501
So the spice rub
is doing two things.

00:01:31.501 --> 00:01:33.534
It's actually, obviously,
creating flavor,

00:01:33.534 --> 00:01:35.300
but it's also becoming
part of the pork.

00:01:35.300 --> 00:01:37.300
It's gonna help form
a crust on the outside.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:38.434
-All right I like this.
Quest, you have

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.634
any questions so far?
-Uh...

00:01:40.634 --> 00:01:41.801
When do we eat?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:43.267
-All right, that's good.

00:01:43.267 --> 00:01:44.734
-All right. So you can see
you get a really nice

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:46.067
spice rib in there.
-Oh, yeah. Look at that.

00:01:46.067 --> 00:01:47.901
Now, I can never make it look
like that if I do it.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.033
-You can't?
-No.

00:01:49.033 --> 00:01:51.234
-What do you mean?
-I don't know. I just --

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.667
You're a pro at this.
-So we're gonna --

00:01:52.667 --> 00:01:55.834
we're gonna put these in the
oven for about 7 or 8 minutes,

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.200
just until they cook through.
-Yep.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:01:58.334
-Okay?
-Perfect.

00:01:58.334 --> 00:01:59.601
All right.
We're gonna leave

00:01:59.601 --> 00:02:01.234
that pan up there.
And then you guys can bring up

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:03.400
your pork, okay?
And I'm gonna make the pan sauce

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.601
that goes in here.
-Okay.

00:02:04.601 --> 00:02:06.000
So we have a little fresh ginger
that goes right

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.501
into the same pan,
a little bit of honey.

00:02:08.501 --> 00:02:10.133
-Yep. Honey.
-Some orange juice.

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:11.200
-Ooh.
-Whoa.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.501
-Oh, yeah.
-Orange juice.

00:02:12.501 --> 00:02:13.634
-Ginger, orange juice,
and honey.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.567
This is if you have a cough.

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:17.100
If you have a cough or a cold.

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:19.334
-And this is Calvados.
You know what Calvados is?

00:02:19.334 --> 00:02:21.300
-Avocado oil?
-Yes, exactly.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:24.601
No, it's actually --
it's like an apple liqueur.

00:02:24.601 --> 00:02:26.300
So, you know,
pork chops, apples.

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.167
-Oh, wow.
-Old school. Okay?

00:02:28.167 --> 00:02:30.033
So we're gonna add
a little Calvados to this.

00:02:30.033 --> 00:02:31.367
And then we're going
to let it cook down.

00:02:31.367 --> 00:02:33.434
And then we're gonna add
a little bit of butter.

00:02:33.434 --> 00:02:36.234
-Oh, God.
-A little bit of butter.

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:39.300
And then some pink peppercorns.
-And pink peppercorns.

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:40.501
-Pink -- [ Laughs ]
Yes.

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.400
-This is unbelievable.
I like all this stuff.

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:44.234
I have all this stuff in my --
in my cupboard.

00:02:44.234 --> 00:02:45.534
-And then a little...
[ Laughter ]

00:02:45.534 --> 00:02:47.601
a little extra butter
for Julia Child.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.400
-Honey, are you finished
with the Calvados?

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.901
-Okay, a little parsley.

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:54.567
And then, Jimmy, you want a
little salt and pepper in here?

00:02:54.567 --> 00:02:56.300
-Yep. How about this?
Do that?

00:02:56.300 --> 00:02:57.901
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, I like that.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:02:59.367
-That's kind of good, right?
-That's very nice.

00:02:59.367 --> 00:03:01.868
-Yeah, you shouldn't do that.
-We call that the essence.

00:03:01.868 --> 00:03:03.367
-Yeah. The essence.
-Very nice. Beautiful.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.601
-Am I supposed to do the same?
-Yes, absolutely.

00:03:05.601 --> 00:03:06.734
Why not?
-Okay.

00:03:06.734 --> 00:03:08.267
-No, no, I made that up.

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:10.734
-Right in here, Quest.
-What are we supposed to do?

00:03:10.734 --> 00:03:12.267
-Okay. Then you're gonna take --

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:13.934
we're gonna spoon the sauce
right on top.

00:03:13.934 --> 00:03:15.400
-Yeah. Look at this.
This is how you do it

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:16.734
like Bobby Flay style.
-This is how you do it.

00:03:16.734 --> 00:03:18.701
Okay.
-Come on, now.

00:03:18.701 --> 00:03:20.367
-Quest, a little bit of sauce
for you, as well.

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.033
-Look at this.
Can you see this?

00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:24.968
-And then you have the fries.
So we have the pork and fries.

00:03:24.968 --> 00:03:26.968
You can have them on the side.
But in France,

00:03:26.968 --> 00:03:28.501
they just serve them
right on the plate like this.

00:03:28.501 --> 00:03:31.067
-Yeah, hey.
-And you have the pork frite.

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.934
-Ooh la la.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:37.133
Bobby Flay, everybody.
His new restaurant, Brasserie B,

00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:40.334
opens in Caesars Palace
in Las Vegas next month

00:03:40.334 --> 00:03:42.434
and "Beat Bobby Flay:
Holiday Throwdown"

00:03:42.434 --> 00:03:44.567
premieres Tuesday
on Food Network.

00:03:44.567 --> 00:03:46.968
More "Tonight Show"
after the break. Stick around.

